EXT. SHELLED FARMHOUSE ROOF, ARDENNES - DAWN

Snow dusts the broken tiles. Beyond the ridge, the thud of far guns.

CORPORAL EUGENE "GENE" BRODSKY (20s, frozen mustache) crouches behind a chimney with binoculars. Beside him, PRIVATE LOUIS TRUDEAU-PARK (19, baby-faced, rifle hugged) shivers. A few yards away, SERGEANT MARGUERITE OYELOWO (30s, tough, her helmet dented) sits against a beam, tying a rag around her wrist.

She tightens it with her teeth. He lowers the binoculars.

GENE
Sarge, I count six.

OYELOWO
Count again.

GENE
Eight.

OYELOWO
Better.

TRUDEAU-PARK
Is it true what they say? About the Tigers?

OYELOWO
Louis, eat your biscuit.

TRUDEAU-PARK
I'm not hungry.

OYELOWO
I didn't ask.

He opens the biscuit tin. His fingers are blue. She reaches over and, without a word, tucks his scarf tighter.

GENE
They're moving.

She rises on one knee and takes the binoculars. Her jaw hardens.

OYELOWO
Gene, wire the others. Louis, with me.

They slide down the roof toward the ladder.
